<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Theudebald, Duke of Alamannia</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">fl. 727–746</span> · <a href="/centuries/8th-century">8th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Theudebald was a duke of the Alemanni in the 730s and 740s, a son of Duke Gotfrid and brother of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lantfrid">Lantfrid</a>. He resisted the Carolingian mayors of the palace, driving <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pirmin">Saint Pirmin</a> out of Reichenau around 727 and repeatedly rising against Frankish rule. He was finally defeated by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pepin-the-short">Pepin the Short</a> and Carloman in the 740s, after which the Alemannic duchy was abolished.</p></div>
